# Candidate ReWorld-Video inference environment: Linux x86_64, CPython 3.10, torch 2.6.0 CUDA 12.4
# (the DriveLaW-Video kit's interpreter, torch build and shared versions). ReWorld vendors no diffusers:
# diffusers comes from PyPI. 0.37.1 is the proposed pin (decision D6 in reworld_pins.json): the release
# code imports diffusers.utils.apply_lora_scale, which first exists in 0.37.0, and the LTX transformer,
# LTX VAE, flow-match scheduler and export_utils files are byte-identical in 0.37.0, 0.37.1 and 0.38.0.
# The official source is NOT pip-installed: its src/ is put on sys.path, exactly as the shipped
# scripts/sample_dualflow_dit.py does. Runtime dependencies of the official pyproject.toml are kept,
# except bitsandbytes (8-bit text-encoder quantisation; the vae_only inference path never imports it).
# This file is resolved without installing packages or downloading model weights.
